  "body": "Found in the Opus brief review for #899 and recorded in PR #925 (2026-10-13 bug bash). Both behaviours predate #925; it did not introduce them. From code reading at master `01c3fa1b`.\n\nLabel artifact files are content-addressed (`artifact-<sha256>`, `services/Labels/ArtifactService.php` ~:76-81), so identical renders share one stored file.\n\n1. **Store reuses a collected artifact.** `Store` looks for an `$existing` artifact with the same content (~:79-82) without checking `collected_at`. An identical re-render after that artifact's preview was collected therefore skips `Put` and creates an artifact row whose bytes are already gone. That artifact is later refused as `artifact_collected`.\n2. **Store does not serialize against collection.** Collection deletes a file's bytes when no other uncollected artifact shares that file. A new sharer whose insert is not yet committed is invisible to that count, so collection can delete the bytes the new artifact is about to reference.\n\n## Done when\n\n- [ ] `Store` never reuses a collected artifact's bytes. It either rewrites the bytes or ignores collected matches.\n- [ ] `Store` and `CollectExpiredPreviews` serialize per file. #925 introduces a per-file advisory try-lock that `Store` could take in blocking form. A two-connection regression test covers it.\n\nRelated: #899, #925, plan 27 piece 6.\n",
